ept_id":"sore_throat","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.32,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":0.5735},"texts":{"dsc:1.113":{"ref":"De materia medica 1.113","headword":"κεράσια καὶ αὐτὰ","lang":"grc","source":"dioscorides","text":"κεράσια καὶ αὐτὰ μὲν χλωρὰ λαμβανόμενα εὐκοίλια τυγχάνει, ξηρὰ δὲ ἵστησι κοιλίαν. τὸ δὲ κόμμι τῶν κεράσων βῆχα χρονίαν ἰᾶται λαμβανόμενον μετὰ κράματος, εὔχροιάν τε καὶ ὀξυδερκίαν καὶ ὄρεξιν ποιεῖ· ὠφελεῖ δὲ καὶ λιθιῶντας μετʼ οἴνου πινόμενον.","spans":[{"start":39,"end":46,"concept_id":"constipation","polarity":"action"},{"start":66,"end":78,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":106,"end":109,"concept_id":"cough","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":169,"end":176,"concept_id":"eye_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":184,"end":188,"concept_id":"appetite_loss","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":212,"end":217,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"}]},"cul:069-the-cherry-tree":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: The Cherry-Tree","headword":"The Cherry-Tree","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"It is a tree of _Venus_. Cherries, as they are of different tastes, so they are of different qualities. The sweet pass through the stomach and the belly more speedily, but are of little nourishment; the tart or sour are more pleasing to an hot stomach, procure appetite to meat, to help and cut tough phlegm, and gross humours; but when these are dried, they are more binding to the belly than when they are fresh, being cooling in hot diseases, and welcome to the stomach, and provokes urine. The gum of the Cherry-tree, desolved in wine is good for a cold, cough, and hoarseness of the throat; mends the colour in the face, sharpens the eye-sight, provokes appetite, and helps to break and expel the stone, and dissolved, the water thereof is much used to break the stone, and to expel gravel and wind.","spans":[{"start":240,"end":251,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":261,"end":269,"concept_id":"appetite_loss","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":368,"end":388,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"action"},{"start":478,"end":492,"concept_id":"diuresis","polarity":"action"},{"start":559,"end":564,"concept_id":"cough","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":570,"end":580,"concept_id":"sore_throat","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":626,"end":648,"concept_id":"eye_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":659,"end":667,"concept_id":"appetite_loss","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":702,"end":707,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":768,"end":773,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":782,"end":803,"concept_id":"flatulence","polarity":"action"}]}},"gloss":{"dsc:1.113":{"39":"loosening the bowels (εὔκοιλιος)","66":"checks ... the bowels","106":"cough (βήξ, βήσσοντες)","169":"sharp-sighted (ὀξυδερκής)","184":"appetite (ὄρεξις)","212":"stone patients, lithiasis (λιθιῶντες, λιθίασις)"},"cul:069-the-cherry-tree":{"240":"weak / cold / hot stomach (dyspepsia)","261":"appetite (provokes / restores)","368":"binds the belly (astringent, antidiarrhoeal)","478":"provokes urine: diuretic","559":"cough, coughs","570":"hoarseness of the throat / voice","626":"clears / sharpens / strengthens the sight","659":"appetite (provokes / restores)","702":"the stone (urinary calculus)","768":"the stone (urinary calculus)","782":"expels / breaks wind (carminative)"}},"images":[]}